IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wirc-regs-dates`

§ `The employer's questions under the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 13 — reimbursement of weekly payments an employer makes first (2013 Act s 179(5)-(7))`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you had to make weekly payments to a worker before the Authority paid you.
-- s 179(5): the employer "must be reimbursed by the Authority"; s 179(7): if the Authority does not reimburse
-- "within the prescribed period", it "is liable to pay the employer interest at the prescribed rate".
-- reg 13: the prescribed period is "the period of 30 days after the day on which the Authority is notified that the
-- employer has made a weekly payment". The day of notification is not counted.

`the prescribed reimbursement period in days` MEANS 30

@export If I made a weekly payment to my worker before the Victorian WorkCover Authority paid me, by what date must the Authority reimburse me before it becomes liable to pay me interest (Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 s 179(7), Regulations reg 13)? (No answer means section 179(5) does not apply to me.)
GIVEN `I had to pay before the Authority paid me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to make the weekly payment to your worker before you received the payment from the Authority? (yes or no)
      `the date the Authority was notified of my payment` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the Authority was notified that you had made the weekly payment
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must the Authority reimburse me` MEANS
    IF `I had to pay before the Authority paid me`
    THEN JUST (`the date days after` `the date the Authority was notified of my payment` `the prescribed reimbursement period in days`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 179(7) is an "if": not reimbursed within the period, liable; reimbursed within it, not (JUST FALSE).
-- NOTHING where s 179(5) does not apply.
@export If I made a weekly payment to my worker before the Victorian WorkCover Authority paid me, is the Authority liable to pay me interest because it did not reimburse me within 30 days of being notified (Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 s 179(7), Regulations reg 13)?
GIVEN `I had to pay before the Authority paid me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to make the weekly payment to your worker before you received the payment from the Authority? (yes or no)
      `the date the Authority was notified of my payment` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the Authority was notified that you had made the weekly payment
      `the Authority has reimbursed me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority reimbursed you for that payment yet? (yes or no)
      `the date I was reimbursed` IS A DATE @desc The date the Authority reimbursed you (ignored if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (used if the Authority has not reimbursed you)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the Authority liable to pay me interest on my weekly payment` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I had to pay before the Authority paid me`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Authority has reimbursed me`
         THEN JUST (NOT (`falls on or before` `the date I was reimbursed` `the last day`))
         ELSE JUST (NOT (`falls on or before` `today` `the last day`))
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            `the date days after` `the date the Authority was notified of my payment` `the prescribed reimbursement period in days`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulations 14 and 15 — contributions by self-insurers (2013 Act s 388)`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you are a self-insurer.
-- s 388(1): "A self-insurer must pay contributions into the WorkCover Authority Fund"; s 388(2): the Authority
-- determines the amount "in accordance with the regulations". The costs and the remuneration of all employers are
-- figures the Authority holds; they are inputs here.

-- reg 14 (until 31 December 2024): [{B/C x D} - {A x B/C}] x 0.6 + {A x B/C}.
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `C` IS A NUMBER, `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 14 formula` `A` `B` `C` `D` MEANS
    `the reduced part` PLUS `the full part`
    WHERE
        `the share` MEANS `B` DIVIDED BY `C`
        `the full part` MEANS `A` TIMES `the share`
        `the reduced part` MEANS ((`the share` TIMES `D`) MINUS `the full part`) TIMES 0.6

-- reg 15 (on and after 1 January 2025): 25 per cent of A/B x C.
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `B` IS A NUMBER, `C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 15 formula` `A` `B` `C` MEANS
    25% TIMES ((`A` DIVIDED BY `B`) TIMES `C`)

`the last day of regulation 14` MEANS Date 31 12 2024

-- "Until 31 December 2024" is read as up to and including that day; reg 15 runs "on and after 1 January 2025".
-- A period the text fixes: outside it the regulation gives no amount (NOTHING, since the answer is a number).
@export As a self-insurer, what contribution into the WorkCover Authority Fund is determined for a quarter up to 31 December 2024, under regulation 14 of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024 (Vic)? (No answer if the determination is after 31 December 2024 or the remuneration total is 0.)
GIVEN `the date of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The date the Authority determines the contribution (regulation 14 applies until 31 December 2024)
      `A the Authority's preceding-quarter costs under s 513(5)(c) and (g) and Division 2 of Part 6` IS A NUMBER @desc A: the costs incurred in the preceding quarter referred to in section 513(5)(c) and (g), plus the Authority's costs that quarter of administering Division 2 of Part 6 (self-insurance), in dollars
      `B my relevant remuneration in the preceding financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc B: the relevant remuneration you paid or had to pay in the preceding financial year, worked out as if you were an employer liable to pay premiums, in dollars
      `C the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers` IS A NUMBER @desc C: the total relevant remuneration of all premium-paying employers plus that of all self-insurers (worked out as for B), in the preceding financial year, in dollars
      `D(a) the preceding-quarter costs under s 513(5)(c), (d), (f), (g) and (l)` IS A NUMBER @desc D(a): the preceding quarter's costs referred to in section 513(5)(c), (d) (without the excluded computer network, premium audit and actuarial costs), (f), (g) and (l), in dollars
      `D(b) the Authority's preceding-quarter costs of administering Division 2 of Part 6` IS A NUMBER @desc D(b): the Authority's costs in the preceding quarter of administering Division 2 of Part 6, in dollars
      `D(c) the Authority's costs of meeting liabilities under s 403` IS A NUMBER @desc D(c): the Authority's costs of meeting any liability incurred under section 403 (the liability for an insolvent self-insurer's claims), in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my quarterly self-insurer contribution under regulation 14` MEANS
    IF     `falls on or before` `the date of the determination` `the last day of regulation 14`
       AND `C the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the regulation 14 formula`
                    `A the Authority's preceding-quarter costs under s 513(5)(c) and (g) and Division 2 of Part 6`
                    `B my relevant remuneration in the preceding financial year`
                    `C the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers`
                    (    `D(a) the preceding-quarter costs under s 513(5)(c), (d), (f), (g) and (l)`
                    PLUS `D(b) the Authority's preceding-quarter costs of administering Division 2 of Part 6`
                    PLUS `D(c) the Authority's costs of meeting liabilities under s 403`))
    ELSE NOTHING

@export As a self-insurer, what contribution into the WorkCover Authority Fund is determined at the start of a calendar year from 2025, under regulation 15 of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2024 (Vic)? (No answer if the determination is before 1 January 2025 or the remuneration total is 0.)
GIVEN `the date of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The date the Authority determines the contribution (regulation 15 applies on and after 1 January 2025, at the start of each calendar year)
      `A(a) the preceding-year costs under s 513(5)(c), (d), (f), (g) and (l)` IS A NUMBER @desc A(a): the preceding financial year's costs referred to in section 513(5)(c), (d) (without the excluded computer network, premium audit, actuarial and self-insurer-ineligible service costs), (f), (g) and (l), in dollars
      `A(b) the Authority's preceding-year costs of administering Division 2 of Part 6` IS A NUMBER @desc A(b): the Authority's costs in the preceding financial year of administering Division 2 of Part 6 (self-insurance), in dollars
      `A(c) the Authority's preceding-year costs of meeting liabilities under s 403` IS A NUMBER @desc A(c): the Authority's costs in the preceding financial year of meeting any liability incurred under section 403, in dollars
      `A(d) earlier years' costs not yet included in a determination` IS A NUMBER @desc A(d): costs of the kinds in A(a) to A(c) from any earlier financial year not included in a previous determination under section 388, in dollars
      `B the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers` IS A NUMBER @desc B: the total relevant remuneration of all premium-paying employers plus that of all self-insurers (worked out as for C), in the preceding financial year, in dollars
      `C my relevant remuneration in the preceding financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc C: the relevant remuneration you paid or had to pay in the preceding financial year, worked out as if you were an employer liable to pay premiums, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my self-insurer contribution under regulation 15` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`falls on or before` `the date of the determination` `the last day of regulation 14`))
       AND `B the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the regulation 15 formula`
                    (    `A(a) the preceding-year costs under s 513(5)(c), (d), (f), (g) and (l)`
                    PLUS `A(b) the Authority's preceding-year costs of administering Division 2 of Part 6`
                    PLUS `A(c) the Authority's preceding-year costs of meeting liabilities under s 403`
                    PLUS `A(d) earlier years' costs not yet included in a determination`)
                    `B the total relevant remuneration of all employers and self-insurers`
                    `C my relevant remuneration in the preceding financial year`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Section 388(3) and (5) — when a self-insurer's contribution is due, and what follows if it is not paid`
-- Situation: this group only arises if you are a self-insurer.
-- s 388(3): a contribution is due on 1 August, 1 November, 1 February and 1 May in each year, subject to (4): the
-- Authority may vary the date. s 388(5): "If a contribution is not paid within 14 days of the due date", it may be
-- recovered as a debt with interest at the prescribed rate and the surcharge in a Ministerial Order (s 380(3)).
-- (The prescribed rate of interest is not in these Regulations: finding 4 in NOTES.md.)

`the days allowed after the due date` MEANS 14

DECLARE `Self-insurer party` IS ONE OF `the self-insurer`
DECLARE `Self-insurer action` IS ONE OF `pays the contribution`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Self-insurer party` `Self-insurer action`
`the duty to pay a contribution` MEANS
    PARTY `the self-insurer`
    MUST `pays the contribution`
    WITHIN `the days allowed after the due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the self-insurer` BECAUSE "contribution not paid within 14 days of the due date: recoverable as a debt with interest and surcharge (s 388(5))"

-- The next of the four due dates on or after a date.
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next due date on or after` `the date` MEANS
    IF `falls on or before` `the date` (Date 1 2 (DATE_YEAR `the date`))
    THEN Date 1 2 (DATE_YEAR `the date`)
    ELSE IF `falls on or before` `the date` (Date 1 5 (DATE_YEAR `the date`))
         THEN Date 1 5 (DATE_YEAR `the date`)
         ELSE IF `falls on or before` `the date` (Date 1 8 (DATE_YEAR `the date`))
              THEN Date 1 8 (DATE_YEAR `the date`)
              ELSE IF `falls on or before` `the date` (Date 1 11 (DATE_YEAR `the date`))
                   THEN Date 1 11 (DATE_YEAR `the date`)
                   ELSE Date 1 2 (DATE_YEAR `the date` PLUS 1)

@export As a self-insurer, when is my next contribution into the WorkCover Authority Fund due under section 388(3) of the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic)? (No answer if the Authority has varied the date.)
GIVEN `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `the Authority has varied my due date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority varied the date on which your contribution is due (s 388(4))? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When is my next self-insurer contribution due` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has varied my due date`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the next due date on or after` `today`)

-- Built on the duty above. s 388(5) is an "if": paid within 14 days of the due date, the contribution cannot be
-- recovered under it (FALSE); not paid by then, it can (TRUE).
@export As a self-insurer, can my contribution be recovered from me as a debt, with interest and a surcharge, because I did not pay it within 14 days of its due date (Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) s 388(5))?
GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE @desc The date the contribution was due (1 August, 1 November, 1 February or 1 May, or the date the Authority set instead)
      `I have paid the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the contribution? (yes or no)
      `the date I paid` IS A DATE @desc The date you paid it (ignored if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (used if you have not paid)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can my contribution be recovered as a debt` MEANS
    IF `I have paid the contribution`
    THEN IF `falls on or before` `the due date` `the date I paid`
         THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the duty to pay a contribution` (`the day number of` `the due date`) (LIST (EVENT `the self-insurer` `pays the contribution` (`the day number of` `the date I paid`)))
              WHEN FULFILLED THEN FALSE
              OTHERWISE TRUE
         ELSE FALSE
    ELSE `days from` `the due date` `to` `today` GREATER THAN `the days allowed after the due date`
